1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,477
You log in.
Your password never reaches your agent.

2
00:00:04,477 --> 00:00:07,977
The API on staging is down. Look at my Conn terminal and get it running again.
You

3
00:00:07,977 --> 00:00:10,279
It asks to join. Once.

4
00:00:10,279 --> 00:00:14,194
It picks up the shell you are already in.

5
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:24,012
On your server, every command waits for you.

6
00:00:24,012 --> 00:00:26,508
It wants to delete the whole cache.

7
00:00:26,508 --> 00:00:27,828
You say no.

8
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:30,698
Then you just type.
Your keystroke takes the terminal back.

9
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:34,398
I cleared the stale lock myself, so keep the cache. Read the terminal and continue.
You

10
00:00:34,398 --> 00:00:41,960
It reads what you did.

11
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:46,870
And finishes the job.

12
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:51,270
The API is back up on :8080. `./api.sh health` returns `{"status": "ok", "cache": "warm"}`, the cache is intact, and I've released control.
Claude Code

13
00:00:47,070 --> 00:00:52,670
Your agent works in your terminal. You keep the keyboard.
Real Conn, a real SSH login and a real Claude Code session in one continuous take. Prepared scenario; still moments shortened.
